WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.871 --> 00:00:04.369
- [Narrator] This is the
Rowley's palm pit viper,

00:00:04.369 --> 00:00:07.369
and it's as dangerous as it is rare.

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:14.000
There are 10 species of palm pit viper

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.771
that inhabit the cloud
forests of Central America.

00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:19.218
But of all of them, the Rowley's

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.815
is the most rare and elusive.

00:00:21.815 --> 00:00:24.946
It can only be found on
three isolated mountains

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:27.226
in southern Mexico.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.682
Brilliant green and slender,

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:30.609
these vipers will spend
most of their lives,

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:34.043
coiled quietly in trees
and other vegetation.

00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:35.587
They are not aggressive by nature,

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:38.070
but will strike if disturbed.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.015
A bite from a Rowley's is not
likely to be fatal to humans,

00:00:41.015 --> 00:00:44.595
but be warned, no
specific anti-venom exists

00:00:44.595 --> 00:00:47.954
for this extraordinary species of snake.

00:00:47.954 --> 00:00:50.114
While not necessarily a threat to us,

00:00:50.114 --> 00:00:52.745
those that should be worried
are the small mammals

00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:55.999
and tree frogs that the viper preys upon.

00:00:55.999 --> 00:01:00.382
Those that stray too close will
meet a swift and silent end.

00:01:00.382 --> 00:01:01.877
But even these venomous predators

00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:04.080
can't stave off bigger threats.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.009
Deforestation and
over-collection for the pet trade

00:01:07.009 --> 00:01:10.151
are perilous threats for this rare animal.

00:01:10.151 --> 00:01:13.151
This is the Rowley's palm pit viper.

